{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"joystick-encoder","name":"Joystick and rotary encoder","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"A thumb joystick (KY-023: two knobs and a push button) and a rotary encoder knob (KY-040: clicks round in steps, and pushes). Work them from the run panel.","category":"Input","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// Joystick: two potentiometers (the stick tilts them) and a push switch to GND.\nbench.device('joystick', (part) => {\n  const x = part.control('x'), y = part.control('y'), press = part.control('press');\n  let v = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      v = io.supply('+5V', 'GND');\n      const gnd = io.v('GND') ?? 0;\n      if (v < 1) { io.release('VRx'); io.release('VRy'); io.connect('SW', 'GND', press.down); return; }\n      // a pot's wiper: between GND and +5V\n      io.drive('VRx', gnd + (v * (x.value + 100)) / 200, 1);\n      io.drive('VRy', gnd + (v * (y.value + 100)) / 200, 1);\n      io.connect('SW', 'GND', press.down);\n      io.draw(0.0005);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (v < 1) return ['no power (+5V)'];\n      return [`x ${x.value}, y ${y.value}${press.down ? ', pushed' : ''}`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n// Rotary encoder: two switches (CLK and DT) on a notched wheel, both open (high) at each notch. One\n// click: both go low and come back high; clockwise, CLK leads and DT follows; anticlockwise, DT leads.\n// (So at each change of CLK, DT different from CLK means clockwise.) The module pulls both up.\nbench.device('encoder-knob', (part) => {\n  const left = part.control('left'), right = part.control('right'), press = part.control('press');\n  const knob = part.motor('knob');\n  let clk = 1, dt = 1, queue = [], next = 0, count = 0, v = 0;\n  const click = (cw) => {\n    const [a, b] = cw ? ['CLK', 'DT'] : ['DT', 'CLK'];\n    queue.push([a, 0], [b, 0], [a, 1], [b, 1]);\n    count += cw ? 1 : -1;\n  };\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      v = io.supply('+', 'GND');\n      for (let i = right.presses(); i > 0; i--) click(true);\n      for (let i = left.presses(); i > 0; i--) click(false);\n      // one change at a time, as a hand turns it\n      if (queue.length && io.time >= next) {\n        const [pin, lv] = queue.shift();\n        if (pin === 'CLK') clk = lv;\n        else dt = lv;\n        next = io.time + 0.025; // (each state lasts a few frames: a program reading it in loop() sees every one)\n      }\n      if (v >= 2.5) {\n        // pulled up by the module, switched to GND by the wheel\n        io.drive('CLK', clk ? v : 0, clk ? 0 : 1);\n        io.drive('DT', dt ? v : 0, dt ? 0 : 1);\n      } else { io.release('CLK'); io.release('DT'); }\n      io.connect('SW', 'GND', press.down);\n      knob.to(count * 18, 5); // (20 clicks a turn)\n    },\n    status() {\n      return [v >= 2.5 ? `${count} clicks from the start${press.down ? ', pushed' : ''}` : 'no power (+)'];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","parts":[{"id":"ky023","name":"Joystick (KY-023)","description":"VRx and VRy give 0 V to +5V's volts as the stick goes left/right and up/down (half in the middle): read them with analogRead. SW joins GND while the stick is pushed in (use INPUT_PULLUP). +5V to 3.3 or 5 V, GND.","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":12,"shape":[{"box":[3.4,0.16,2.6],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"box":[1.6,1,1.6],"at":[0.3,0.66,0],"color":"#2a2c31"},{"cyl":[0.18,1],"at":[0.3,1.6,0],"color":"#2a2c31"},{"cyl":[0.9,0.6],"at":[0.3,2.3,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["GND","+5V","VRx","VRy","SW"],"at":[-1.6,0,-0.508],"dir":"z","kinds":{"GND":"gnd","+5V":"vin","VRx":"out","VRy":"out","SW":"out"},"extra":{"+5V":{"label":"+5V (3.3-5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5}}}],"controls":[{"id":"x","kind":"slider","label":"Left / right","min":-100,"max":100,"step":1,"value":0},{"id":"y","kind":"slider","label":"Down / up","min":-100,"max":100,"step":1,"value":0},{"id":"press","kind":"button","label":"Push in"}],"device":"joystick"},{"id":"ky040","name":"Rotary encoder (KY-040)","description":"A knob that clicks round (20 clicks a turn, no end). Each click, CLK goes low and back high; at each change of CLK, DT different from CLK means clockwise. SW joins GND while pushed (use INPUT_PULLUP). + to 3.3 or 5 V (it pulls CLK and DT up), GND. Turn it from the run panel.","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":10,"shape":[{"box":[2,0.16,2.6],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"box":[1.3,0.7,1.3],"at":[0,0.51,0.3],"color":"#b9bec7"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["GND","+","SW","DT","CLK"],"at":[-0.508,0,-1.1],"kinds":{"GND":"gnd","+":"vin","SW":"out","DT":"out","CLK":"out"},"extra":{"+":{"label":"+ (3.3-5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},"CLK":{"pulled":"up"},"DT":{"pulled":"up"}}}],"moving":[{"id":"knob","mass":3,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.6,1.4],"at":[0,1.56,0.3],"color":"#2a2c31"},{"box":[0.12,0.05,0.5],"at":[0,2.28,0.55],"color":"#f2f2f2"}],"joint":{"type":"turn","at":[0,0.86,0.3],"axis":[0,-1,0],"motor":"stepper","torque":0.3,"speed":120,"volts":5}}],"controls":[{"id":"left","kind":"button","label":"Click left"},{"id":"right","kind":"button","label":"Click right"},{"id":"press","kind":"button","label":"Push"}],"device":"encoder-knob"}],"examples":[{"name":"Joystick steers a servo","description":"Move the joystick's left/right slider in the run panel: a servo follows; push it in to centre the servo.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Joystick steers a servo","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-6,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"stick","type":"joystick-encoder/ky023","name":"Joystick","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[4,0,-5],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"servo","type":"servo-sg90","name":"Servo","params":{"start":0},"parent":null,"pos":[5,0,5],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"stick","pin":"+5V"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"stick","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"A0"},"b":{"uid":"stick","pin":"VRx"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"stick","pin":"SW"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"servo","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#f08c2a"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"5V"},"b":{"uid":"servo","pin":"V+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"servo","pin":"GND"},"color":"#6b4226"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// The servo follows the joystick's left/right; pushing the stick in centres it.\n// (The joystick runs on 3.3 V, so its middle is half of the board's 0-4095 reading.)\n#include <Servo.h>\n\n#define STICK_X A0\n#define STICK_SW 3\n\nServo servo;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(STICK_SW, INPUT_PULLUP);\n  servo.attach(15);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  int x = analogRead(STICK_X);\n  int angle = map(x, 0, 4095, 0, 180);\n  if (digitalRead(STICK_SW) == LOW) angle = 90;\n  servo.write(angle);\n  delay(20);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Encoder counts","description":"Click the encoder left and right in the run panel: the count goes down and up in the serial monitor; push to reset it.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Encoder counts","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-6,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"enc","type":"joystick-encoder/ky040","name":"Encoder","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[4,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"enc","pin":"+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"enc","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"enc","pin":"CLK"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"enc","pin":"DT"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP4"},"b":{"uid":"enc","pin":"SW"},"color":"#3fbf7f"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Count the encoder's clicks: right = up, left = down, push = back to 0.\n#define CLK 2\n#define DT 3\n#define SW 4\n\nint counter = 0;\nint lastClk;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(CLK, INPUT);\n  pinMode(DT, INPUT);\n  pinMode(SW, INPUT_PULLUP);\n  lastClk = digitalRead(CLK);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  int clk = digitalRead(CLK);\n  if (clk != lastClk && clk == HIGH) {     // CLK came back up: one click done\n    if (digitalRead(DT) != clk) counter++;  // DT lagging behind: clockwise\n    else counter--;\n    Serial.print(\"count: \");\n    Serial.println(counter);\n  }\n  lastClk = clk;\n  if (digitalRead(SW) == LOW && counter != 0) {\n    counter = 0;\n    Serial.println(\"reset\");\n  }\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}